Game Setup &
Standard Turn
<BOLD>1.</BOLD> First, choose somebody to Host the game. This should be a player that is  familiar with the game. It is the job of the Host to run the game. The Host may take the Host card to show their status as the Host.
<BOLD>2.</BOLD> The Host should select as many cards as there are players. For inexperienced players, check Card Mix on more details on how to pick cards. They will then deal one card to each player, face-down. The players look at their own card, but may not share it with other players.
<BOLD>3.</BOLD> The Host then puts the town to sleep and the first night begins. Depending on the cards in play, the Host wakes up certain roles. For more details, check the action order at the end of the booklet.
<BOLD>4.</BOLD> After all roles have used their abilities, the Host wakes the town up and reveals who has died. The players that have died reveal their card (if playing with flips) and are no longer allowed to participate in the game.
<BOLD>5.</BOLD> The players now have a chance to debate.
<BOLD>6.</BOLD> When enough time has passed, the Host will end the discussion and start the vote. All players will need to point at another player they want to eliminate at the same time. The player with the most votes is eliminated. If there is a tie, nobody is eliminated.
<BOLD>7.</BOLD> The players now fall asleep again, and the next night begins.
